  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<size=135%><color=#382C30><b>Privacy Policy</b></color></size>\nLast updated:
    10 November 2026\n\n<size=108%><b>1. Introduction</b></size>\nGlowUp (\"we\",
    \"our\", or \"us\") respects your privacy and is committed to protecting your
    personal data. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and
    safeguard your information when you use our mobile application. Please read this
    privacy policy carefully. If you do not agree with the terms of this privacy
    policy, please do not access the application.\n\n<size=108%><b>2. Information
    We Collect</b></size>\nWe collect information that you voluntarily provide to
    us when registering for an account and while using the application. This includes:\n\n<indent=4%>-
    Personal Identifiers: your first name, middle name, last name, date of birth,
    age, and email address.</indent>\n<indent=4%>- Profile and Preference Data: your
    skin type, skin tone, skin conditions, and known cosmetic allergens and sensitivities.
    This information is used exclusively to tailor the app's safety analyses and
    product recommendations to your personal profile.</indent>\n<indent=4%>- Scan
    Data: the ingredient text read from product labels, the results of each analysis,
    the products you save to your Recent Scans, and any names you give them.</indent>\n<indent=4%>-
    Suggestions: skin conditions, allergens, or ingredients you add that are not
    yet in our lists, so that we can review them and improve the database.</indent>\n<indent=4%>-
    Technical Data: our cloud provider may process basic technical information, such
    as your IP address and device identifiers, in order to deliver and secure the
    service.</indent>\n\n<size=108%><b>3. How We Use Your Information</b></size>\nHaving
    accurate information permits us to provide you with a smooth, efficient, and
    customized experience. Specifically, we use information collected via GlowUp
    to:\n\n<indent=4%>- Create and secure your user account using Google Firebase
    Authentication.</indent>\n<indent=4%>- Confirm that the email address is yours.
    When you sign up with an email and password, your account is created as soon
    as the first sign-up page is filled in, and Google Firebase Authentication sends
    a message with a link to that address. The sign-up goes on once you have tapped
    the link. If you leave the sign-up before finishing it, that unfinished account
    is removed again.</indent>\n<indent=4%>- Make sure the email address you sign
    up with can really receive email. For an address that is not from a well-known
    provider, the app asks a public internet directory (DNS, run by Google or Cloudflare)
    whether the part after the @ (for example \"school.edu.ph\") has a mail server.
    Only that part is sent, never your name or the whole address. Temporary (\"throw-away\")
    email addresses cannot be used to sign up.</indent>\n<indent=4%>- Store and retrieve
    your profile preferences securely using Google Cloud Firestore.</indent>\n<indent=4%>-
    Personalize cosmetic ingredient safety assessments and filter recommendations
    based on your registered skin type, skin conditions, age, and allergies.</indent>\n<indent=4%>-
    Keep your scan history available across sessions and, when you are online, across
    your devices.</indent>\n<indent=4%>- Count how often a brand is scanned, without
    attaching your name to that count, so that we can prioritise which products to
    add to the database.</indent>\n<indent=4%>- Communicate with you regarding account
    updates, security alerts, and support messages.</indent>\n\n<size=108%><b>4.
    Camera, Scans, and AR Try-On</b></size>\nGlowUp asks for permission to use your
    camera for two features: scanning a product and its ingredient list, and previewing
    shades on your face with AR Try-On.\n\n<indent=4%>- The text on a product is
    read on your device. We do not record or store the live camera feed. We keep
    a photo only when you choose to send one for a product that is not in our catalog
    yet (see \"Product Photo Submissions\" below).</indent>\n<indent=4%>- For a scan,
    only the text that was read, the product's name and the result are kept and analysed.
    When you are online and the app cannot name the product by itself, a few still
    pictures of the PRODUCT you are holding (its front, back or bottom; four at most,
    once per scan) may be sent to our AI service provider so that the product can
    be recognised (see section 5). Those pictures are not saved by us.</indent>\n<indent=4%>-
    So that the app knows a product again the next time you scan it, it keeps what
    its pack looks like as a set of numbers (not a picture; the picture cannot be
    rebuilt from them), together with any other name you typed for the product. These
    stay on your device only and are removed when you clear the app's data or uninstall
    the app.</indent>\n<indent=4%>- For AR Try-On, the picture of your face is used
    only while the preview is on screen. It is not saved and it is never sent to
    us or to anyone else.</indent>\n\nYou can withdraw camera permission at any time
    in your device settings. The scanning and try-on features will stop working until
    permission is given again, but you can still type ingredients in by hand.\n\n<size=108%><b>Product
    Photo Submissions</b></size>\nWhen a product you scan is not in our catalog yet,
    you can choose to take one photo of it and send it to us. Nothing is sent unless
    you tap \"Use photo\", and the app tells you before your first photo is sent
    that GlowUp will review it.\n\n<indent=4%>- What is stored: the photo, cut on
    your device to the part that shows the product (the rest of the picture is discarded
    before anything is sent); the text the app read on the product; the product's
    brand, name, type and shade; the ingredient list and the web address of the page
    it came from, or the list printed on the pack; the time you sent it; and your
    account id.</indent>\n<indent=4%>- Who sees it: GlowUp administrators, who review
    it in our admin portal. You can see your own photo; other app users cannot.</indent>\n<indent=4%>-
    Why: to identify the product, to find its published ingredient list, and to add
    the product to our catalog after an administrator has checked it. Until then
    it is shown to you as \"Unverified \u2014 pending review\".</indent>\n<indent=4%>-
    How it is processed: the cut photo and the text read on it are sent to our AI
    service provider only to recognise which product it is. The ingredient list is
    never written by the AI: it is taken from product pages our server opens (the
    brand's own website first, then retailers) or from the list printed on your pack.
    Ingredient data from the web may be incomplete.</indent>\n<indent=4%>- How long
    it is kept: the photo is deleted when an administrator approves or rejects the
    entry. The product details stay in our catalog once approved; they carry no information
    about you. If you want your photo or entry removed earlier, contact us (section
    12).</indent>\n<indent=4%>- Where it is kept: in our Google Firebase database,
    protected by security rules that let only you and GlowUp administrators read
    the photo.</indent>\n\n<size=108%><b>5. AI-Assisted Analysis</b></size>\nPart
    of each analysis is produced automatically. When you are online, the following
    may be sent to our AI service provider: up to four still pictures of the product,
    the text read from it, the product's name, and ingredient names. This is used
    to recognise the product, to find its published ingredient list, and to describe
    ingredients that are not yet in our database. The product's name may also be
    sent to the FDA Philippines verification site to check whether the product is
    registered. When the camera read the product's barcode, that barcode (and nothing
    else) may be sent to Open Beauty Facts, a public list of cosmetics, to compare
    its ingredient list with the one the app has.\n\nYour profile is never sent to
    the AI service. Your name, email address, password, age, skin type, skin tone,
    skin conditions, and allergens stay out of every such request: the comparison
    between a product and your profile is made on your device.\n\nAutomated results
    can be incomplete or wrong. Please read section 4 of the Terms and Conditions
    below.\n\n<size=108%><b>6. Data Security and Third-Party Services</b></size>\nWe
    implement industry-standard security measures, including encrypted transit layers
    (HTTPS) and salted password hashing, to protect your personal information. Your
    password is never stored in readable form. We utilize Google Firebase as our
    primary cloud backend infrastructure. Google Firebase adheres to rigorous security
    standards. We do not sell, trade, or otherwise transfer your personally identifiable
    information to outside parties.\n\nNo method of transmission or storage is completely
    secure. We cannot guarantee absolute security, and you use the application with
    that understanding.\n\n<size=108%><b>7. Offline Use</b></size>\nTo let GlowUp
    work without an internet connection, a copy of your profile, your scan history,
    and the ingredient database is kept on your device. Changes you make offline
    are sent to the cloud the next time you are online. If you share your device
    with other people, sign out when you are finished.\n\nThe email addresses that
    have signed in with a password on this device are also kept on the device, so
    that the log-in page can offer them under the email field. You can take an address
    off that list there at any time, and it is removed when you delete your account
    or clear the app's data in your phone's settings. Only the address is kept: passwords
    are never shown, offered, or stored in readable form. The app shows this list
    of its own instead of your phone's saved accounts.\n\n<size=108%><b>8. Data Retention
    and Account Deletion</b></size>\nWe retain your personal data only for as long
    as your account is active or as needed to provide you with app services. You
    can delete your account yourself at any time: open Settings and choose Delete
    My Account (you need an internet connection and your password). This removes
    your profile, your scan history and your sign-in from our database, and everything
    about the account on your phone. You can also ask our support team to delete
    it.\n\nA few things are kept apart from your profile and are not removed by Delete
    My Account: the anonymous scan counts (they carry no name, email or account id),
    and the skin conditions, allergens, ingredients or product photos you sent us
    as suggestions, which carry your account id until our team has reviewed them.
    Ask our support team if you want those removed too.\n\n<size=108%><b>9. Children's
    Privacy</b></size>\nGlowUp is not intended for children under 13 years of age,
    and we do not knowingly collect personal data from them. If you believe a child
    under 13 has created an account, please contact us so that we can remove it.\n\n<size=108%><b>10.
    Your Rights and Choices</b></size>\nGlowUp follows the Data Privacy Act of 2012
    (Republic Act No. 10173) of the Philippines. Under that law you have the right
    to be informed about how your personal data is used, to see the data we hold
    about you, to correct it, to object to its use, to ask for it to be deleted or
    blocked, to receive a copy of it, to be compensated for damage caused by misuse
    of it, and to withdraw your consent at any time. You can update your profile
    in the app, delete your account in Settings, and contact us for anything else.
    If you think your data was handled wrongly, you may also complain to the National
    Privacy Commission (privacy.gov.ph).\n\nYour skin type, skin tone, skin conditions
    and allergens are information about your health. The law treats such information
    as sensitive personal information, so we use it only with your clear consent.
    You give that consent with the second box on the page where you accept this policy,
    and you can withdraw it by deleting your account. Without that consent the app
    cannot compare products with your profile.\n\nYour data is stored with Google
    Firebase (Google Cloud), whose servers are outside the Philippines. Google keeps
    it under its own security and data protection terms.\n\nIf a security breach
    puts your personal data at risk of serious harm, we will tell you and the National
    Privacy Commission within 72 hours of knowing about it, and say what happened
    and what you can do.\n\n<size=108%><b>11. Changes to This Policy</b></size>\nWe
    may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will change
    the \"Last updated\" date at the top and, where the change is significant, tell
    you inside the app.\n\n<size=108%><b>12. Contact Us</b></size>\nYou can send
    a report from the app: Settings > Contact support. The report goes to the GlowUp
    team through our support dashboard, not by email. It contains the kind of report
    you chose (Bug, Wrong scan result or Other), your message, your account id, the
    app version and your phone model. Your last scan (the product, the result shown
    and the ingredients read) is included only when you switch on \"Include my last
    scan\". Only GlowUp administrators can read reports.\n\nIf you have questions
    about this Privacy Policy, you can also contact our support team at: GlowUpAdminSupport@gmail.com\n\n\n<size=135%><color=#382C30><b>Terms
    and Conditions</b></color></size>\n\n<size=108%><b>1. Acceptance of Terms</b></size>\nBy
    downloading, installing, or creating an account on GlowUp, you agree to be bound
    by these Terms and Conditions. If you disagree with any part of these terms,
    you must discontinue use of the application immediately.\n\n<size=108%><b>2.
    Eligibility</b></size>\nYou must be at least 13 years old to use GlowUp. If you
    are under 18, you confirm that a parent or guardian has read and agreed to these
    terms on your behalf.\n\n<size=108%><b>3. Medical and Dermatological Disclaimer</b></size>\n<indent=4%>-
    Not a Medical Device: GlowUp is designed strictly as a cosmetic safety and ingredient-analysis
    tool. It is not a medical device, clinical diagnostic tool, or a substitute for
    professional dermatological advice, diagnosis, or treatment.</indent>\n<indent=4%>-
    Consult a Professional: always seek the advice of a licensed dermatologist or
    qualified healthcare provider with any questions you may have regarding a medical
    skin condition, severe dermatitis, or acute allergic reactions. Never disregard
    professional medical advice or delay in seeking it because of information provided
    by GlowUp.</indent>\n<indent=4%>- Patch Testing: cosmetic formulations react
    differently across individuals. Users are strongly advised to perform a patch
    test on a small area of skin before applying any new skincare product, regardless
    of the app's safety result or ingredient analysis.</indent>\n\n<size=108%><b>4.
    Ingredient Analysis and AI Results</b></size>\nThe results shown by GlowUp are
    generated automatically from the text read off a product label, from our ingredient
    database, and from an AI service. They are provided for general information only.\n\n<indent=4%>-
    The camera can misread a label, and manufacturers change their formulas. Always
    check the ingredient list printed on the product you actually hold.</indent>\n<indent=4%>-
    An ingredient that is not yet in our database is not part of the result. A result
    of \"safe\" means that nothing in our records conflicts with your profile. It
    is not a guarantee that you will not react to the product.</indent>\n<indent=4%>-
    A result of \"caution\" or \"harmful\" is a prompt to look more closely or to
    ask a professional. It is not a diagnosis.</indent>\n\n<size=108%><b>5. AR Try-On</b></size>\nAR
    Try-On shows a simulated preview. Colours and finish depend on your screen, your
    camera, and the lighting around you, and the real product may look different
    on your skin. The preview is not a promise of how a product will look or perform.\n\n<size=108%><b>6.
    Product Information and Recommendations</b></size>\nProduct, brand, and ingredient
    information is supplied by our team and by third parties and may be incomplete
    or out of date. A recommendation in the app is not an endorsement, and we do
    not guarantee that a recommended product is available where you live.\n\n<size=108%><b>7.
    User Accounts and Responsibilities</b></size>\n<indent=4%>- You are responsible
    for maintaining the confidentiality of your login credentials and password.</indent>\n<indent=4%>-
    You agree to provide accurate, current, and complete information during the onboarding
    and registration process and to keep your profile updated.</indent>\n<indent=4%>-
    You agree not to use the app for any unlawful purpose or in any way that could
    damage, disable, or impair the application's infrastructure.</indent>\n\n<size=108%><b>8.
    Acceptable Use</b></size>\nYou agree not to copy or extract the database in bulk,
    attempt to bypass the security of the application, use the application to harass
    or harm another person, or submit content that is unlawful, misleading, or that
    you do not have the right to share.\n\n<size=108%><b>9. Your Suggestions</b></size>\nWhen
    you suggest a skin condition, allergen, ingredient, or product, you allow us
    to review it, edit it, and add it to the database so that other users can benefit
    from it. Do not include personal or confidential information in a suggestion.\n\n<size=108%><b>10.
    Intellectual Property Rights</b></size>\nThe GlowUp name, logo, source code,
    design elements, and underlying software are the intellectual property of the
    developers. You may not copy, modify, distribute, or reverse-engineer any portion
    of this application without express written permission.\n\n<size=108%><b>11.
    Third-Party Services</b></size>\nGlowUp relies on services operated by other
    companies, including Google Firebase and, if you choose to use them, the Google
    sign-in service. Your use of those services is also subject to their own terms
    and privacy policies.\n\n<size=108%><b>12. Suspension and Termination</b></size>\nYou
    may stop using GlowUp at any time. We may suspend or close an account that breaks
    these terms or that puts the service or other users at risk.\n\n<size=108%><b>13.
    Limitation of Liability</b></size>\nTo the maximum extent permitted by applicable
    law, the creators and operators of GlowUp shall not be held liable for any direct,
    indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages resulting from your use
    of the application, including but not limited to adverse skin reactions, allergic
    flare-ups, or reliance on ingredient analysis data. Use the application at your
    own risk.\n\n<size=108%><b>14. Changes to These Terms</b></size>\nWe may update
    these Terms and Conditions from time to time. If you continue to use GlowUp after
    a change takes effect, you accept the updated terms.\n\n<size=108%><b>15. Governing
    Law</b></size>\nThese terms are governed by the laws of the country in which
    the operator of GlowUp is established, without affecting any consumer protection
    rights you have under the law of the country where you live.\n\n<size=108%><b>16.
    Contact</b></size>\nTo report a problem, use Settings > Contact support in the
    app: your report is received by the GlowUp team through the support dashboard
    (see section 12 of the Privacy Policy for what a report contains). Questions
    about these Terms and Conditions can also be sent to: GlowUpAdminSupport@gmail.com\n\n<size=108%><b>17.
    Credits</b></size>\n<indent=4%>- The sound played when a scan is removed in Recent
    Scans is \"Teeth Chattering - Sound Effect\", as shared by the YouTube channel
    Sound Library (youtube.com/watch?v=enz7eXF5IUo). Its original creator is not
    known.</indent>\n<indent=4%>- Ingredient lists marked \"Open Beauty Facts\" come
    from Open Beauty Facts (openbeautyfacts.org), a public database made by volunteers
    and shared under the Open Database Licence.</indent>\n\nThank you for reading.
    Tick the box below to confirm that you have read and agree to the Privacy Policy
    and the Terms and Conditions.\n\n"
